/-!
# Picard excision and line-bundle specialization on regular models

Let `R` be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field `K` and residue field `k`, and let
`toBase : X ⟶ Spec R` be a proper regular integral Noetherian scheme of dimension at most two
whose generic point lies over the generic point of `Spec R`.

This file compares line bundles across the generic fibre `X_K`, the model `X`, the special fibre
`X_s`, the reduced special fibre `(X_s)_red = V(√(𝔪·𝒪_X))`, and the component curves `C_i` of
`X_s`, and constructs the Picard specialization map of
[Stacks, Tag 0CE7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CE7):

1. **Generic-fibre Picard excision.** Over a one-dimensional local domain `R` which is not a field,
   the open immersion `genericFiberι R K toBase : X_K ⟶ X` has image `{x : X | toBase x ≠ s}`
   (`TauCeti.range_genericFiberι`), the complement of the special fibre. When `R` is a discrete
   valuation ring and `X` has factorial local rings (in particular when `X` is regular of
   dimension at most two), restriction `Pic(X) → Pic(X_K)` is surjective and its kernel is the
   subgroup generated by the vertical component line bundles `[𝒪_X(C_i)]`
   (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.pullback_genericFiberι_surjective_of_isRegular` and
   `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.pullback_genericFiberι_eq_one_iff_of_isRegular`).
2. **Multidegree comparison across `X`, `X_s`, and `(X_s)_red`.** Every component `C_i` factors
   through `(X_s)_red` and `X_s`. Dividing the intersection numbers `(L · C_i)_k` by the component
   weights `w_i = [κ_i : k]` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberWeight`) defines compatible
   multidegree homomorphisms `reducedSpecialFiberMultidegree`, `specialFiberMultidegreeOnFiber`,
   and `specialFiberMultidegree` into `Component → ℤ`. On `[𝒪_X(C_i)]`, the multidegree is the
   `i`-th row of the weighted intersection matrix `a'_{ij} = a_{ij} / w_j`
   (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix`).
3. **Generic-fibre Picard specialization and torsion lifting.** Because vertical classes map onto
   the row space of `a'_{ij}`, `specialFiberMultidegree` descends along `Pic(X) → Pic(X_K)` to
   `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberPicardSpecialization` with values in the cokernel
   `(Component → ℤ) ⧸ range(vecMulLinear A')`. Its kernel consists precisely of generic-fibre line
   bundles extending to a model line bundle of multidegree zero on `(X_s)_red`
   (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.mem_ker_specialFiberPicardSpecialization_iff`). When `X` is flat
   over `R` and `X_s` is connected, any vertical class of multidegree zero has order dividing the
   greatest common divisor of the component multiplicities `m_i`, yielding unique `n`-torsion
   multidegree-zero model extensions whenever `n` is coprime to that greatest common divisor
   (`Scheme.Hom.existsUnique_torsion_of_mem_ker_specialFiberPicardSpecialization`).

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.reducedSpecialFiberMultidegree`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberMultidegreeOnFiber`, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberMultidegree`: compatible multidegree homomorphisms on
  `Pic((X_s)_red)`, `Pic(X_s)`, and `Pic(X)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix`: the matrix
  `a'_{ij} = a_{ij} / w_j` of component degrees over their constant fields.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberPicardSpecialization`: the specialization homomorphism
  from `Pic(X_K)` to the cokernel of the weighted intersection matrix.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.range_genericFiberι`: the generic fibre is the complement of the special fibre.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.pullback_genericFiberι_surjective_of_isRegular` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.pullback_genericFiberι_eq_one_iff_of_isRegular`: exactness of
  `Vertical → Pic(X) → Pic(X_K) → 1`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberMultidegree_prod_zpow`: the multidegree of
  `∏_i [𝒪_X(C_i)]^{v_i}` is `v ᵥ* A'`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.mem_ker_specialFiberPicardSpecialization_iff`: characterization of
  `ker specialFiberPicardSpecialization` by multidegree-zero extensions to `X`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.exists_dvd_specialFiberMultiplicity_and_pow_eq_one` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.existsUnique_torsion_of_mem_ker_specialFiberPicardSpecialization`:
  control of the vertical multidegree-zero kernel and unique `n`-torsion lifting to `Pic^{[0]}(X)`.

## References

* [The Stacks Project, Tag 0C9U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C9U),
  [Tag 0C7H](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C7H),
  [Tag 0CE7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CE7), and
  [Tag 01WS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WS).
* Q. Liu, *Algebraic Geometry and Arithmetic Curves*, Section 9.1.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry IsLocalRing Order
open scoped Matrix
open TauCeti TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
open AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData (vanishingIdeal
  isEffectiveCartier_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular)

universe u

namespace TauCeti

/-- **The generic fibre is the complement of the special fibre.** Over a local domain `R` of Krull
dimension at most one which is not a field, with fraction ring `K`, a point of `X` lies in the
image of `genericFiberι R K toBase` if and only if it does not map to the closed point of
`Spec R`. -/
theorem range_genericFiberι (R K : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsLocalRing R]
    [Ring.DimensionLEOne R] [CommRing K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K]
    (hR : maximalIdeal R ≠ ⊥) {X : Scheme.{u}} (toBase : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) :
    Set.range (genericFiberι R K toBase) = {x : X | toBase x ≠ closedPoint R} := by
  have hr : Set.range (genericFiberι R K toBase) = toBase ⁻¹' {genericPoint (Spec (.of R))} :=
    calc Set.range (genericFiberι R K toBase)
        = Set.range (genericFiberι R K toBase ∘
            (genericFiberIsoFiberGenericPoint (K := K) toBase).inv) :=
          ((genericFiberIsoFiberGenericPoint (K := K) toBase).inv.surjective.range_comp _).symm
      _ = Set.range ((genericFiberIsoFiberGenericPoint (K := K) toBase).inv ≫
            genericFiberι R K toBase) :=
          congrArg Set.range (funext fun x ↦ (Scheme.Hom.comp_apply _ _ x).symm)
      _ = Set.range (toBase.fiberι (genericPoint (Spec (.of R)))) :=
          congrArg (fun g : toBase.fiber (genericPoint (Spec (.of R))) ⟶ X ↦ Set.range g)
            (genericFiberIsoFiberGenericPoint_inv_genericFiberι toBase)
      _ = toBase ⁻¹' {genericPoint (Spec (.of R))} :=
          Scheme.Hom.range_fiberι toBase (genericPoint (Spec (.of R)))
  rw [hr]
  ext x
  change toBase x = genericPoint (Spec (.of R)) ↔ toBase x ≠ closedPoint R
  rw [genericPoint_eq_bot_of_affine]
  refine ⟨fun h hc ↦ hR ?_, fun h ↦ PrimeSpectrum.ext (by_contra fun hne ↦ h ?_)⟩
  · exact (congrArg PrimeSpectrum.asIdeal (h.symm.trans hc)).symm
  · exact PrimeSpectrum.ext (IsLocalRing.eq_maximalIdeal ((toBase x).isPrime.isMaximal hne))

/-- Over a discrete valuation ring `R` with fraction ring `K`, the range of `genericFiberι` is the
complement of the special fibre. -/
theorem range_genericFiberι_of_isDiscreteValuationRing (R K : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing R] [CommRing K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (toBase : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) :
    Set.range (genericFiberι R K toBase) = {x : X | toBase x ≠ closedPoint R} :=
  range_genericFiberι R K (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_a_field R) toBase

/-- Composing an inclusion of closed subschemes contained in the special fibre with
`subschemeToSpecialFiber` gives `subschemeToSpecialFiber` on the smaller subscheme. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
lemma inclusion_subschemeToSpecialFiber {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} {toBase : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)} {I J : X.IdealSheafData}
    (hI : (specialFiberι R toBase).ker ≤ I) (hIJ : I ≤ J) :
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.inclusion hIJ ≫ subschemeToSpecialFiber hI =
      subschemeToSpecialFiber (hI.trans hIJ) := by
  have := isClosedImmersion_specialFiberι R toBase
  rw [← cancel_mono (specialFiberι R toBase), Category.assoc,
    subschemeToSpecialFiber_specialFiberι, Scheme.IdealSheafData.inclusion_subschemeι,
    subschemeToSpecialFiber_specialFiberι]

end TauCeti

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

/-! ### Reduced special fibre and generic-fibre Picard excision -/

section ReducedAndGenericFiber

/-- The closure of a point of the special fibre, with its reduced structure, is a closed subscheme
of the reduced special fibre `V(√(𝔪·𝒪_X))`. -/
theorem ker_radical_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] {X : Scheme.{u}} (toBase : X ⟶ Spec (.of R))
    {x : X} (hx : toBase x = closedPoint R) :
    (specialFiberι R toBase).ker.radical ≤
      vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {x}, isClosed_closure⟩ := by
  have hrad : (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {x}, isClosed_closure⟩).radical =
      vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {x}, isClosed_closure⟩ :=
    (Scheme.IdealSheafData.isReduced_subscheme_iff_radical_eq _).mp inferInstance
  rw [← hrad]
  intro U
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.radical_ideal, Scheme.IdealSheafData.radical_ideal]
  exact Ideal.radical_mono (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton hx U)

variable {R : Type u} (K : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsDiscreteValuationRing R]
  [CommRing K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K] {X : Scheme.{u}} (toBase : X ⟶ Spec (.of R))

/-- If `X` has a point outside the special fibre over a discrete valuation ring `R`, its generic
fibre `X_K` is nonempty. -/
theorem nonempty_genericFiber_of_base_ne_closedPoint {x : X} (hx : toBase x ≠ closedPoint R) :
    Nonempty (genericFiber R K toBase).left := by
  have hx' : x ∈ Set.range (genericFiberι R K toBase) := by
    rw [range_genericFiberι_of_isDiscreteValuationRing]
    exact hx
  obtain ⟨y, -⟩ := hx'
  exact ⟨y⟩

variable [IsIntegral X] [IsNoetherian X]

/-- **Surjectivity of restriction to the generic fibre on Picard groups.** Let `X` be a Noetherian
integral scheme with factorial local rings over a discrete valuation ring `R` with fraction ring
`K`, whose generic point lies outside the special fibre. Every line-bundle class on `X_K` extends
to `X`. -/
theorem pullback_genericFiberι_surjective
    [∀ x : X, UniqueFactorizationMonoid (X.presheaf.stalk x)]
    (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R) :
    Function.Surjective (LineBundleClass.pullback (genericFiberι R K toBase)) := by
  have := isOpenImmersion_genericFiberι R K toBase
  have := toBase.nonempty_genericFiber_of_base_ne_closedPoint K hη
  exact LineBundleClass.pullback_surjective_of_isOpenImmersion (genericFiberι R K toBase)

/-- **Kernel of restriction to the generic fibre on Picard groups.** Under the hypotheses of
`pullback_genericFiberι_surjective`, a line-bundle class on `X` restricts to `1` on `X_K` if and
only if it is a product of integer powers of the component classes `[𝒪_X(C_i)]` of the special
fibre. -/
theorem pullback_genericFiberι_eq_one_iff
    [∀ x : X, UniqueFactorizationMonoid (X.presheaf.stalk x)]
    (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R) {a : LineBundleClass X} :
    LineBundleClass.pullback (genericFiberι R K toBase) a = 1 ↔
      ∃ v : (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
          (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset → ℤ,
        a = ∏ i, LineBundleClass.primeDivisorClass i.1 ^ v i := by
  have := isOpenImmersion_genericFiberι R K toBase
  have := toBase.nonempty_genericFiber_of_base_ne_closedPoint K hη
  refine LineBundleClass.pullback_eq_one_iff_exists_prod_of_isOpenImmersion
    (genericFiberι R K toBase) fun η ↦ ?_
  rw [Set.Finite.mem_toFinset, range_genericFiberι_of_isDiscreteValuationRing]
  change toBase η = closedPoint R ↔ ¬ toBase η ≠ closedPoint R
  exact not_not.symm

/-- **Surjectivity of `Pic(X) → Pic(X_K)` on a regular model.** On a regular Noetherian integral
scheme `X` of dimension at most two over a discrete valuation ring `R` with generic point outside
the special fibre, restriction `Pic(X) → Pic(X_K)` is surjective. -/
theorem pullback_genericFiberι_surjective_of_isRegular
    [TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegular X] (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2)
    (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R) :
    Function.Surjective (LineBundleClass.pullback (genericFiberι R K toBase)) :=
  have := fun x ↦ TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegular.uniqueFactorizationMonoid_stalk x (hX x)
  toBase.pullback_genericFiberι_surjective K hη

/-- **Exact kernel of `Pic(X) → Pic(X_K)` on a regular model.** On a regular Noetherian integral
scheme `X` of dimension at most two over a discrete valuation ring `R` with generic point outside
the special fibre, a line-bundle class on `X` restricts to `1` on `X_K` if and only if it is a
product `∏_i [𝒪_X(C_i)]^{v_i}` supported on the irreducible components `C_i` of the special
fibre. -/
theorem pullback_genericFiberι_eq_one_iff_of_isRegular
    [TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegular X] (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2)
    (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R) {a : LineBundleClass X} :
    LineBundleClass.pullback (genericFiberι R K toBase) a = 1 ↔
      ∃ v : (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
          (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset → ℤ,
        a = ∏ i, (LineBundleClass.mk
          (isEffectiveCartier_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular hX
            i.1.2).toInvertibleSheaf)⁻¹ ^ v i := by
  have := isOpenImmersion_genericFiberι R K toBase
  have := toBase.nonempty_genericFiber_of_base_ne_closedPoint K hη
  refine LineBundleClass.pullback_eq_one_iff_exists_prod_of_isOpenImmersion_of_isRegular
    (genericFiberι R K toBase) hX fun η ↦ ?_
  rw [Set.Finite.mem_toFinset, range_genericFiberι_of_isDiscreteValuationRing]
  change toBase η = closedPoint R ↔ ¬ toBase η ≠ closedPoint R
  exact not_not.symm

end ReducedAndGenericFiber

/-! ### Multidegrees across `X`, `X_s`, and `(X_s)_red`, and the weighted intersection matrix -/

section Multidegree

section General

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [Ring.DimensionLEOne R]
  {X : Scheme.{u}} (toBase : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [IsIntegral X] [IsNoetherian X] [IsProper toBase]
  (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2) (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R)
  (h₀ : ∀ (η : CodimensionOnePoint X) (hc : toBase η = closedPoint R),
    letI := subschemeOverResidueField
      (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton hc)
    FiniteDimensional (ResidueField R) (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
      (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(η : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 0))
  (h₁ : ∀ (η : CodimensionOnePoint X) (hc : toBase η = closedPoint R),
    letI := subschemeOverResidueField
      (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton hc)
    FiniteDimensional (ResidueField R) (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
      (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(η : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1))

/-- Helper constructing the multidegree homomorphism `Additive (LineBundleClass Y) →+ (_ → ℤ)` for
any scheme `Y` receiving morphisms from the special-fibre components `C_i`. -/
private def componentMultidegreeHom {Y : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : ∀ i : (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
        (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset,
      (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme ⟶ Y) :
    Additive (LineBundleClass Y) →+
      ((toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
          (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset → ℤ) where
  toFun a i :=
    letI := subschemeOverResidueField
      (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
        ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))
    LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber (ResidueField R) (f i) a.toMul /
      (toBase.specialFiberWeight ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2) : ℤ)
  map_zero' := by
    funext i
    let := subschemeOverResidueField
      (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
        ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))
    rw [toMul_zero, LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber_one, Int.zero_ediv]
    rfl
  map_add' a b := by
    funext i
    have hi : toBase i.1 = closedPoint R := (Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2
    let := subschemeOverResidueField
      (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton hi)
    have := isProper_subschemeOverResidueField
      (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton hi)
    have := toBase.relativeDimensionLE_subscheme_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton hX
      (fun h ↦ one_ne_zero (i.1.2.symm.trans (coheight_eq_zero.mpr h))) hi
    have := h₀ i.1 hi
    have := h₁ i.1 hi
    have hdvd : (toBase.specialFiberWeight hi : ℤ) ∣
        LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber (ResidueField R) (f i) a.toMul := by
      rw [specialFiberWeight_def]
      exact LineBundleClass.finrank_cohomology_zero_trivial_dvd_intersectionNumber (ResidueField R)
        (f i) (toBase.isField_globalSections_subscheme_closure_singleton hi) a.toMul
    rw [toMul_add, LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber_mul_of_isIntegral,
      Int.add_ediv_of_dvd_left hdvd, Pi.add_apply]

/-- The **multidegree on the reduced special fibre** `(X_s)_red = V(√(𝔪·𝒪_X))`, sending a
line-bundle class `c` to the tuple of degrees `deg_{κ_i}(c|_{C_i}) = (c · C_i)_k / w_i` on the
irreducible components `C_i` over their constant fields `κ_i`. -/
def reducedSpecialFiberMultidegree :
    Additive (LineBundleClass (specialFiberι R toBase).ker.radical.subscheme) →+
      ((toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
          (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset → ℤ) :=
  toBase.componentMultidegreeHom hX hη h₀ h₁ fun i ↦
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.inclusion
      (toBase.ker_radical_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
        ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))

/-- Componentwise formula for `reducedSpecialFiberMultidegree`. -/
@[simp]
theorem reducedSpecialFiberMultidegree_apply
    (c : Additive (LineBundleClass (specialFiberι R toBase).ker.radical.subscheme)) (i) :
    toBase.reducedSpecialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁ c i =
      letI := subschemeOverResidueField
        (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
          ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))
      LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber (ResidueField R)
        (Scheme.IdealSheafData.inclusion
          (toBase.ker_radical_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
            ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))) c.toMul /
        (toBase.specialFiberWeight ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2) : ℤ) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The **multidegree on the scheme-theoretic special fibre** `X_s`, sending a line-bundle class on
`X_s` to its component degrees `deg_{κ_i}(b|_{C_i})` over the component constant fields. -/
def specialFiberMultidegreeOnFiber :
    Additive (LineBundleClass (specialFiber R toBase).left) →+
      ((toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
          (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset → ℤ) :=
  toBase.componentMultidegreeHom hX hη h₀ h₁ fun i ↦
    subschemeToSpecialFiber
      (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
        ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))

/-- Componentwise formula for `specialFiberMultidegreeOnFiber`. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberMultidegreeOnFiber_apply
    (b : Additive (LineBundleClass (specialFiber R toBase).left)) (i) :
    toBase.specialFiberMultidegreeOnFiber hX hη h₀ h₁ b i =
      letI := subschemeOverResidueField
        (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
          ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))
      LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber (ResidueField R)
        (subschemeToSpecialFiber
          (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
            ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))) b.toMul /
        (toBase.specialFiberWeight ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2) : ℤ) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The **special-fibre multidegree** of a line-bundle class on the model `X`, sending `a` to the
tuple `i ↦ (a · C_i)_k / w_i` of degrees of `a|_{C_i}` over the constant fields `κ_i` of the
components. -/
def specialFiberMultidegree :
    Additive (LineBundleClass X) →+
      ((toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
          (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset → ℤ) :=
  toBase.componentMultidegreeHom hX hη h₀ h₁ fun i ↦
    (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subschemeι

/-- Componentwise formula for `specialFiberMultidegree`. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberMultidegree_apply (a : Additive (LineBundleClass X)) (i) :
    toBase.specialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁ a i =
      letI := subschemeOverResidueField
        (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
          ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))
      LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber (ResidueField R)
        (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subschemeι a.toMul /
        (toBase.specialFiberWeight ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2) : ℤ) :=
  (rfl)

/-- `specialFiberMultidegreeOnFiber` factors through restriction from `X_s` to `(X_s)_red`. -/
theorem specialFiberMultidegreeOnFiber_eq_reducedSpecialFiberMultidegree_pullback
    (b : LineBundleClass (specialFiber R toBase).left) :
    toBase.specialFiberMultidegreeOnFiber hX hη h₀ h₁ (Additive.ofMul b) =
      toBase.reducedSpecialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁
        (Additive.ofMul (LineBundleClass.pullback
          (subschemeToSpecialFiber (specialFiberι R toBase).ker.le_radical) b)) := by
  funext i
  let := subschemeOverResidueField
    (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
      ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))
  rw [specialFiberMultidegreeOnFiber_apply, reducedSpecialFiberMultidegree_apply, toMul_ofMul,
    toMul_ofMul, LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber_pullback, inclusion_subschemeToSpecialFiber]

/-- `specialFiberMultidegree` factors through restriction from `X` to `X_s`. -/
theorem specialFiberMultidegree_eq_specialFiberMultidegreeOnFiber_pullback
    (a : LineBundleClass X) :
    toBase.specialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁ (Additive.ofMul a) =
      toBase.specialFiberMultidegreeOnFiber hX hη h₀ h₁
        (Additive.ofMul (LineBundleClass.pullback (specialFiberι R toBase) a)) := by
  funext i
  let := subschemeOverResidueField
    (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
      ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))
  rw [specialFiberMultidegree_apply, specialFiberMultidegreeOnFiber_apply, toMul_ofMul,
    toMul_ofMul, LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber_pullback,
    subschemeToSpecialFiber_specialFiberι]

/-- `specialFiberMultidegree` factors through restriction from `X` to `(X_s)_red`. -/
theorem specialFiberMultidegree_eq_reducedSpecialFiberMultidegree_pullback
    (a : LineBundleClass X) :
    toBase.specialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁ (Additive.ofMul a) =
      toBase.reducedSpecialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁
        (Additive.ofMul
          (LineBundleClass.pullback (specialFiberι R toBase).ker.radical.subschemeι a)) := by
  funext i
  let := subschemeOverResidueField
    (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
      ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))
  rw [specialFiberMultidegree_apply, reducedSpecialFiberMultidegree_apply, toMul_ofMul,
    toMul_ofMul, LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber_pullback,
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.inclusion_subschemeι]

/-- Multiplying the `i`-th coordinate of `specialFiberMultidegree a` by the weight `w_i` recovers
the intersection number `(a · C_i)_k` over the residue field. -/
theorem specialFiberMultidegree_mul_specialFiberWeight (a : Additive (LineBundleClass X)) (i) :
    toBase.specialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁ a i *
        (toBase.specialFiberWeight ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2) : ℤ) =
      letI := subschemeOverResidueField
        (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
          ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))
      LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber (ResidueField R)
        (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subschemeι a.toMul := by
  have hi : toBase i.1 = closedPoint R := (Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2
  let := subschemeOverResidueField
    (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton hi)
  rw [specialFiberMultidegree_apply]
  apply Int.ediv_mul_cancel
  rw [specialFiberWeight_def]
  exact LineBundleClass.finrank_cohomology_zero_trivial_dvd_intersectionNumber (ResidueField R) _
    (toBase.isField_globalSections_subscheme_closure_singleton hi) a.toMul

/-- A line-bundle class on `X` has special-fibre multidegree zero if and only if its intersection
number with every component `C_i` of the special fibre vanishes. -/
theorem specialFiberMultidegree_eq_zero_iff (a : LineBundleClass X) :
    toBase.specialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁ (Additive.ofMul a) = 0 ↔
      ∀ i : (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
          (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset,
        letI := subschemeOverResidueField
          (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
            ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))
        LineBundleClass.intersectionNumber (ResidueField R)
          (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subschemeι a = 0 := by
  refine ⟨fun h i ↦ ?_, fun h ↦ funext fun i ↦ ?_⟩
  · have hm := toBase.specialFiberMultidegree_mul_specialFiberWeight hX hη h₀ h₁
      (Additive.ofMul a) i
    rw [h, Pi.zero_apply, zero_mul, toMul_ofMul] at hm
    exact hm.symm
  · rw [specialFiberMultidegree_apply, toMul_ofMul, h i, Int.zero_ediv, Pi.zero_apply]

end General

section RegularMatrix

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [Ring.DimensionLEOne R]
  {X : Scheme.{u}} (toBase : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [IsIntegral X] [IsNoetherian X]
  [TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegular X]

/-- The **weighted intersection matrix** `a'_{ij} = a_{ij} / w_j` of the special fibre of a regular
model, whose `(i, j)`-entry is the intersection number `(C_j · C_i)_k` divided by the weight `w_j`
of `C_j`. When `A` is symmetric (`specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_isSymm`), `a_{ij} = (C_i · C_j)_k`
is divisible by `w_j` and `a'_{ij}` is the degree of `𝒪_X(C_i)|_{C_j}` over the constant field
`κ_j = H⁰(C_j, 𝒪_{C_j})`. -/
def specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2)
    (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R) :
    Matrix (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
        (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset
      (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
        (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset ℤ :=
  Matrix.of fun i j ↦
    toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη i j /
      (toBase.specialFiberWeight ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp j.2) : ℤ)

/-- Entrywise formula for `specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix`. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix_apply (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2)
    (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R) (i j) :
    toBase.specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix hX hη i j =
      toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη i j /
        (toBase.specialFiberWeight ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp j.2) : ℤ) :=
  (rfl)

variable [IsProper toBase] (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2)
  (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R)
  (h₀ : ∀ (η : CodimensionOnePoint X) (hc : toBase η = closedPoint R),
    letI := subschemeOverResidueField
      (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton hc)
    FiniteDimensional (ResidueField R) (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
      (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(η : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 0))
  (h₁ : ∀ (η : CodimensionOnePoint X) (hc : toBase η = closedPoint R),
    letI := subschemeOverResidueField
      (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton hc)
    FiniteDimensional (ResidueField R) (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
      (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(η : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1))

include h₀ h₁ in
/-- The weight `w_j` of `C_j` divides every entry `a_{ij}` in column `j` of the intersection
matrix, by symmetry of `A` and `specialFiberWeight_dvd_specialFiberIntersectionMatrix`. -/
theorem specialFiberWeight_dvd_specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_right (i j) :
    (toBase.specialFiberWeight ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp j.2) : ℤ) ∣
      toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη i j := by
  have hsym : toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη i j =
      toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη j i :=
    (toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_isSymm hX hη h₀ h₁).apply j i
  rw [hsym]
  exact toBase.specialFiberWeight_dvd_specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη j i

include h₀ h₁ in
/-- Exactness of the division defining `specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix`: multiplying column
`j` by `w_j` recovers `specialFiberIntersectionMatrix`. -/
theorem specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix_mul_specialFiberWeight (i j) :
    toBase.specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix hX hη i j *
        (toBase.specialFiberWeight ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp j.2) : ℤ) =
      toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη i j :=
  Int.ediv_mul_cancel
    (toBase.specialFiberWeight_dvd_specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_right hX hη h₀ h₁ i j)

/-- **Multidegree of a component line bundle.** The multidegree of `[𝒪_X(C_i)]` is the `i`-th row
of `specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix`. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberMultidegree_inv_mk_toInvertibleSheaf (i) :
    toBase.specialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁
        (Additive.ofMul (LineBundleClass.mk
          (isEffectiveCartier_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular hX
            i.1.2).toInvertibleSheaf)⁻¹) =
      toBase.specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix hX hη i := by
  funext j
  have hsym : toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη j i =
      toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη i j :=
    (toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_isSymm hX hη h₀ h₁).apply i j
  rw [specialFiberMultidegree_apply, toMul_ofMul,
    ← toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_apply hX hη j i, hsym,
    specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix_apply]

/-- **Multidegree of a vertical divisor class.** For any integer vector `v` on the special-fibre
components, the multidegree of `∏_i [𝒪_X(C_i)]^{v_i}` is `v ᵥ* A'`. -/
theorem specialFiberMultidegree_prod_zpow
    (v : (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
        (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset → ℤ) :
    toBase.specialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁
        (Additive.ofMul (∏ i, (LineBundleClass.mk
          (isEffectiveCartier_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular hX
            i.1.2).toInvertibleSheaf)⁻¹ ^ v i)) =
      v ᵥ* toBase.specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix hX hη := by
  have hprod : Additive.ofMul (∏ i : (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
          (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset,
        (LineBundleClass.mk
          (isEffectiveCartier_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular hX
            i.1.2).toInvertibleSheaf)⁻¹ ^ v i) =
      ∑ i, v i • Additive.ofMul (LineBundleClass.mk
        (isEffectiveCartier_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular hX
          i.1.2).toInvertibleSheaf)⁻¹ :=
    (ofMul_prod _ _).trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ofMul_zpow _ _)
  rw [hprod, map_sum]
  funext j
  rw [Finset.sum_apply, Matrix.vecMul, dotProduct]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_
  rw [map_zsmul, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, specialFiberMultidegree_inv_mk_toInvertibleSheaf]

end RegularMatrix

end Multidegree

/-! ### Generic-fibre Picard specialization and torsion lifting -/

section Specialization

variable {R : Type u} (K : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsDiscreteValuationRing R]
  [CommRing K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K] {X : Scheme.{u}} (toBase : X ⟶ Spec (.of R))
  [IsIntegral X] [IsNoetherian X] [TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegular X] [IsProper toBase]
  (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2) (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R)
  (h₀ : ∀ (η : CodimensionOnePoint X) (hc : toBase η = closedPoint R),
    letI := subschemeOverResidueField
      (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton hc)
    FiniteDimensional (ResidueField R) (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
      (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(η : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 0))
  (h₁ : ∀ (η : CodimensionOnePoint X) (hc : toBase η = closedPoint R),
    letI := subschemeOverResidueField
      (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton hc)
    FiniteDimensional (ResidueField R) (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
      (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(η : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1))

/-- Every model line-bundle class in the kernel of `Pic(X) → Pic(X_K)` has multidegree in the row
space of `specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix`. -/
theorem specialFiberMultidegree_mem_range_of_pullback_genericFiberι_eq_one {a : LineBundleClass X}
    (ha : LineBundleClass.pullback (genericFiberι R K toBase) a = 1) :
    toBase.specialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁ (Additive.ofMul a) ∈
      LinearMap.range (toBase.specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix hX hη).vecMulLinear := by
  obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ := (toBase.pullback_genericFiberι_eq_one_iff_of_isRegular K hX hη).mp ha
  exact ⟨v, (toBase.specialFiberMultidegree_prod_zpow hX hη h₀ h₁ v).symm⟩

omit [IsProper toBase] in
include hX hη in
/-- Surjectivity of the additive generic-fibre pullback homomorphism on `LineBundleClass`. -/
private lemma toAdditive_pullbackHom_genericFiberι_surjective :
    Function.Surjective
      (MonoidHom.toAdditive (LineBundleClass.pullbackHom (genericFiberι R K toBase))) := by
  intro b
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := toBase.pullback_genericFiberι_surjective_of_isRegular K hX hη b.toMul
  refine ⟨Additive.ofMul a, Additive.toMul.injective ?_⟩
  rw [MonoidHom.toAdditive_apply_apply, LineBundleClass.pullbackHom_apply, toMul_ofMul]
  exact ha

/-- The **Picard specialization homomorphism**
([Stacks, Tag 0CE7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CE7)) from the Picard group of the
generic fibre `X_K` to the cokernel of the weighted intersection matrix `A'`, obtained by lifting a
class on `X_K` to the regular model `X` and taking its multidegree on `(X_s)_red` modulo vertical
classes. -/
def specialFiberPicardSpecialization :
    Additive (LineBundleClass (genericFiber R K toBase).left) →+
      (((toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
            (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset → ℤ) ⧸
        LinearMap.range (toBase.specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix hX hη).vecMulLinear) := by
  let p : Additive (LineBundleClass X) →+
      Additive (LineBundleClass (genericFiber R K toBase).left) :=
    MonoidHom.toAdditive (LineBundleClass.pullbackHom (genericFiberι R K toBase))
  let S := LinearMap.range (toBase.specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix hX hη).vecMulLinear
  let φ : Additive (LineBundleClass X) →+ _ ⧸ S :=
    S.mkQ.toAddMonoidHom.comp (toBase.specialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁)
  have hker : ∀ a ∈ p.ker, φ a = 0 := fun a ha ↦ by
    have ha' : LineBundleClass.pullback (genericFiberι R K toBase) a.toMul = 1 := by
      have h0 := congrArg Additive.toMul (AddMonoidHom.mem_ker.mp ha)
      rwa [MonoidHom.toAdditive_apply_apply, LineBundleClass.pullbackHom_apply, toMul_ofMul,
        toMul_zero] at h0
    rw [AddMonoidHom.comp_apply, LinearMap.toAddMonoidHom_coe, Submodule.mkQ_apply,
      Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero, ← ofMul_toMul a]
    exact toBase.specialFiberMultidegree_mem_range_of_pullback_genericFiberι_eq_one K hX hη h₀ h₁
      ha'
  exact (QuotientAddGroup.lift p.ker φ hker).comp
    (QuotientAddGroup.liftEquiv p.ker
      (toBase.toAdditive_pullbackHom_genericFiberι_surjective K hX hη) rfl).symm.toAddMonoidHom

/-- `specialFiberPicardSpecialization` sends the restriction of `a : LineBundleClass X` to the
quotient class of `specialFiberMultidegree a`. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberPicardSpecialization_pullback (a : LineBundleClass X) :
    toBase.specialFiberPicardSpecialization K hX hη h₀ h₁
        (Additive.ofMul (LineBundleClass.pullback (genericFiberι R K toBase) a)) =
      Submodule.Quotient.mk
        (toBase.specialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁ (Additive.ofMul a)) := by
  let p : Additive (LineBundleClass X) →+
      Additive (LineBundleClass (genericFiber R K toBase).left) :=
    MonoidHom.toAdditive (LineBundleClass.pullbackHom (genericFiberι R K toBase))
  have hp := toBase.toAdditive_pullbackHom_genericFiberι_surjective K hX hη
  have hpa : Additive.ofMul (LineBundleClass.pullback (genericFiberι R K toBase) a) =
      p (Additive.ofMul a) := by
    apply Additive.toMul.injective
    rw [MonoidHom.toAdditive_apply_apply, LineBundleClass.pullbackHom_apply, toMul_ofMul]
    rfl
  have hsymm : (QuotientAddGroup.liftEquiv p.ker hp rfl).symm (p (Additive.ofMul a)) =
      QuotientAddGroup.mk (Additive.ofMul a) :=
    (QuotientAddGroup.liftEquiv p.ker hp rfl).injective <| by
      rw [AddEquiv.apply_symm_apply, QuotientAddGroup.liftEquiv_mk]
  rw [specialFiberPicardSpecialization, hpa, AddMonoidHom.comp_apply, AddEquiv.coe_toAddMonoidHom,
    hsymm]
  rfl

/-- **Exact kernel of `specialFiberPicardSpecialization`**
([Stacks, Tag 0CE7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CE7)). A line-bundle class `b` on the
generic fibre `X_K` lies in the kernel of `specialFiberPicardSpecialization` if and only if it
extends to a line-bundle class `a` on the regular model `X` whose multidegree on `(X_s)_red` is
zero. -/
theorem mem_ker_specialFiberPicardSpecialization_iff
    {b : LineBundleClass (genericFiber R K toBase).left} :
    Additive.ofMul b ∈ (toBase.specialFiberPicardSpecialization K hX hη h₀ h₁).ker ↔
      ∃ a : LineBundleClass X,
        LineBundleClass.pullback (genericFiberι R K toBase) a = b ∧
          toBase.specialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁ (Additive.ofMul a) = 0 := by
  refine ⟨fun hb ↦ ?_, fun ⟨a, haK, ha⟩ ↦ ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨a₀, rfl⟩ := toBase.pullback_genericFiberι_surjective_of_isRegular K hX hη b
    rw [AddMonoidHom.mem_ker, specialFiberPicardSpecialization_pullback,
      Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero, LinearMap.mem_range] at hb
    obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := hb
    let vert : LineBundleClass X :=
      ∏ i, (LineBundleClass.mk
        (isEffectiveCartier_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular hX
          i.1.2).toInvertibleSheaf)⁻¹ ^ v i
    have hvert_pull : LineBundleClass.pullback (genericFiberι R K toBase) vert = 1 :=
      (toBase.pullback_genericFiberι_eq_one_iff_of_isRegular K hX hη).mpr ⟨v, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨a₀ * vert⁻¹, ?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [LineBundleClass.pullback_mul, LineBundleClass.pullback_inv, hvert_pull, inv_one, mul_one]
    · rw [ofMul_mul, ofMul_inv, map_add, map_neg,
        toBase.specialFiberMultidegree_prod_zpow hX hη h₀ h₁ v,
        ← Matrix.vecMulLinear_apply, hv, add_neg_cancel]
  · rw [← haK, AddMonoidHom.mem_ker, specialFiberPicardSpecialization_pullback, ha,
      Submodule.Quotient.mk_zero]

section Connected

variable [Flat toBase] {π : R}

include h₀ h₁ in
/-- On a regular proper flat model with connected special fibre, an integer vector `v` in the left
kernel of `specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix` is a rational multiple of the multiplicity
vector `m`. -/
private lemma exists_rat_mul_specialFiberMultiplicity_of_vecMul_eq_zero
    (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π})
    (hconn : _root_.IsPreconnected (toBase ⁻¹' {closedPoint R}))
    {v : (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
        (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset → ℤ}
    (hv : v ᵥ* toBase.specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix hX hη = 0) :
    ∃ c : ℚ, ∀ j, (v j : ℚ) = c * (toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π j : ℚ) := by
  have hreg : IsSMulRegular R π :=
    IsSMulRegular.of_ne_zero (toBase.ne_zero_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη hπ)
  have hAv : toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη *ᵥ v = 0 := by
    funext j
    have hsym (i) : toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη j i =
        toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη i j :=
      (toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_isSymm hX hη h₀ h₁).apply i j
    have hw := congrArg (· * (toBase.specialFiberWeight
      ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp j.2) : ℤ)) (congrFun hv j)
    rw [Pi.zero_apply, zero_mul, Matrix.vecMul, dotProduct, Finset.sum_mul] at hw
    rw [Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct, Pi.zero_apply, ← hw]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_
    rw [hsym i,
      ← toBase.specialFiberWeightedIntersectionMatrix_mul_specialFiberWeight hX hη h₀ h₁ i j,
      mul_comm _ (v i), ← mul_assoc]
  have hquad : (fun j ↦ (v j : ℚ)) ⬝ᵥ
      (toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη).map (Int.cast : ℤ → ℚ) *ᵥ
        (fun j ↦ (v j : ℚ)) = 0 := by
    have hmul : (toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη).map (Int.cast : ℤ → ℚ) *ᵥ
        (fun j ↦ (v j : ℚ)) = 0 := by
      funext j
      have h := congrArg (Int.cast : ℤ → ℚ) (congrFun hAv j)
      rw [Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct, Pi.zero_apply, Int.cast_zero, Int.cast_sum] at h
      rw [Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct, Pi.zero_apply, ← h]
      exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ by rw [Matrix.map_apply, Int.cast_mul]
    rw [hmul, dotProduct_zero]
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (toBase.dotProduct_mulVec_specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_eq_zero_iff
    hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn (fun j ↦ (v j : ℚ))).mp hquad
  exact ⟨c, fun j ↦ hc j⟩

/-- **Isotropic vertical kernel on a connected special fibre.** On a regular proper flat model with
connected special fibre `X_s = ∑_i m_i C_i`, any model line-bundle class `a` that is trivial on
`X_K` and has multidegree zero on `(X_s)_red` satisfies `a ^ d = 1` for a positive integer `d`
dividing the multiplicity `m_j` of every component `C_j`. -/
theorem exists_dvd_specialFiberMultiplicity_and_pow_eq_one
    (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π})
    (hconn : _root_.IsPreconnected (toBase ⁻¹' {closedPoint R}))
    {a : LineBundleClass X}
    (haK : LineBundleClass.pullback (genericFiberι R K toBase) a = 1)
    (ha0 : toBase.specialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁ (Additive.ofMul a) = 0) :
    ∃ d : ℕ, 0 < d ∧
      (∀ j : (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
          (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset,
        d ∣ toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π j) ∧
      a ^ d = 1 := by
  have hreg : IsSMulRegular R π :=
    IsSMulRegular.of_ne_zero (toBase.ne_zero_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη hπ)
  obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ := (toBase.pullback_genericFiberι_eq_one_iff_of_isRegular K hX hη).mp haK
  rw [toBase.specialFiberMultidegree_prod_zpow hX hη h₀ h₁ v] at ha0
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := toBase.exists_rat_mul_specialFiberMultiplicity_of_vecMul_eq_zero
    hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hconn ha0
  have hrel (j) : v j * (c.den : ℤ) = c.num * (toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π j : ℤ) := by
    refine Int.cast_injective (α := ℚ) ?_
    rw [Int.cast_mul, Int.cast_mul, Int.cast_natCast, Int.cast_natCast, hc j, mul_right_comm,
      Rat.mul_den_eq_num]
  refine ⟨c.den, c.den_pos, fun j ↦ ?_, ?_⟩
  · have hdvdZ : (c.den : ℤ) ∣ c.num * (toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π j : ℤ) :=
      ⟨v j, (hrel j).symm.trans (mul_comm _ _)⟩
    have hdvdN : c.den ∣ c.num.natAbs * toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π j := by
      have h := Int.natAbs_dvd_natAbs.mpr hdvdZ
      rwa [Int.natAbs_natCast, Int.natAbs_mul, Int.natAbs_natCast] at h
    exact c.reduced.symm.dvd_of_dvd_mul_left hdvdN
  · have hpow (i) :
        ((LineBundleClass.mk
          (isEffectiveCartier_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular hX
            i.1.2).toInvertibleSheaf)⁻¹ ^ v i) ^ c.den =
        ((LineBundleClass.mk
          (isEffectiveCartier_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton_of_isRegular hX
            i.1.2).toInvertibleSheaf)⁻¹ ^ toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π i) ^ c.num := by
      rw [← zpow_natCast, ← zpow_mul, hrel i, mul_comm c.num, zpow_mul, zpow_natCast]
    have hsp := toBase.prod_inv_mk_toInvertibleSheaf_vanishingIdeal_pow_eq_one hX hη hπ hreg
    rw [← Finset.prod_coe_sort] at hsp
    refine ((Finset.prod_pow Finset.univ c.den _).symm.trans
      (Finset.prod_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ hpow i)).trans ?_
    exact (Finset.prod_zpow _ Finset.univ c.num).trans (by rw [hsp, one_zpow])

/-- An `n`-torsion model line bundle on a regular proper flat model with connected special fibre
that restricts to `1` on `X_K` and has multidegree `0` on `(X_s)_red` is trivial whenever `n` is
coprime to every common divisor of the component multiplicities. -/
theorem eq_one_of_pullback_genericFiberι_eq_one_of_coprime_specialFiberMultiplicity
    (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π})
    (hconn : _root_.IsPreconnected (toBase ⁻¹' {closedPoint R}))
    {n : ℕ}
    (hcop : ∀ d : ℕ,
      (∀ j : (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
          (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset,
        d ∣ toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π j) → Nat.Coprime n d)
    {a : LineBundleClass X}
    (haK : LineBundleClass.pullback (genericFiberι R K toBase) a = 1)
    (ha0 : toBase.specialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁ (Additive.ofMul a) = 0)
    (han : a ^ n = 1) : a = 1 := by
  obtain ⟨d, -, hdvd, had⟩ :=
    toBase.exists_dvd_specialFiberMultiplicity_and_pow_eq_one K hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hconn haK ha0
  have hnd : ((n : ℤ) * Nat.gcdA n d + (d : ℤ) * Nat.gcdB n d) = 1 := by
    rw [← Nat.gcd_eq_gcd_ab n d, (hcop d hdvd).gcd_eq_one, Nat.cast_one]
  calc a = a ^ (1 : ℤ) := (zpow_one a).symm
    _ = a ^ ((n : ℤ) * Nat.gcdA n d + (d : ℤ) * Nat.gcdB n d) := by rw [hnd]
    _ = (a ^ n) ^ Nat.gcdA n d * (a ^ d) ^ Nat.gcdB n d := by
        rw [zpow_add, zpow_mul, zpow_mul, zpow_natCast, zpow_natCast]
    _ = 1 := by rw [han, had, one_zpow, one_zpow, mul_one]

/-- **Unique `n`-torsion multidegree-zero lifting**
([Stacks, Tag 0CE7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CE7)). On a regular proper flat model
with connected special fibre `X_s = ∑_i m_i C_i`, if `n` is coprime to every common divisor of the
multiplicities `m_i` (in particular for every `n` when `X_s` is reduced, or for `n` coprime to
`char k` when `gcd_i m_i` is a power of `char k`), every `n`-torsion generic-fibre class `b` in
`ker specialFiberPicardSpecialization` admits a unique `n`-torsion extension `a` to `X` of
multidegree zero on `(X_s)_red`. -/
theorem existsUnique_torsion_of_mem_ker_specialFiberPicardSpecialization
    (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π})
    (hconn : _root_.IsPreconnected (toBase ⁻¹' {closedPoint R}))
    {n : ℕ}
    (hcop : ∀ d : ℕ,
      (∀ j : (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
          (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset,
        d ∣ toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π j) → Nat.Coprime n d)
    {b : LineBundleClass (genericFiber R K toBase).left} (hbn : b ^ n = 1)
    (hbker : Additive.ofMul b ∈ (toBase.specialFiberPicardSpecialization K hX hη h₀ h₁).ker) :
    ∃! a : LineBundleClass X,
      LineBundleClass.pullback (genericFiberι R K toBase) a = b ∧
        toBase.specialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁ (Additive.ofMul a) = 0 ∧
        a ^ n = 1 := by
  obtain ⟨a₀, ha₀K, ha₀0⟩ :=
    (toBase.mem_ker_specialFiberPicardSpecialization_iff K hX hη h₀ h₁).mp hbker
  have ha₀nK : LineBundleClass.pullback (genericFiberι R K toBase) (a₀ ^ n) = 1 := by
    rw [LineBundleClass.pullback_pow, ha₀K, hbn]
  have ha₀n0 : toBase.specialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁ (Additive.ofMul (a₀ ^ n)) = 0 := by
    rw [ofMul_pow, map_nsmul, ha₀0, smul_zero]
  obtain ⟨d, -, hdvd, hadn⟩ :=
    toBase.exists_dvd_specialFiberMultiplicity_and_pow_eq_one K hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hconn ha₀nK ha₀n0
  have hnd : (d : ℤ) * Nat.gcdB n d = 1 - (n : ℤ) * Nat.gcdA n d := by
    have h := Nat.gcd_eq_gcd_ab n d
    rw [(hcop d hdvd).gcd_eq_one, Nat.cast_one] at h
    omega
  let a : LineBundleClass X := a₀ ^ ((d : ℤ) * Nat.gcdB n d)
  have haK : LineBundleClass.pullback (genericFiberι R K toBase) a = b := by
    rw [LineBundleClass.pullback_zpow, ha₀K, hnd, zpow_sub, zpow_one, zpow_mul, zpow_natCast,
      hbn, one_zpow, inv_one, mul_one]
  have ha0 : toBase.specialFiberMultidegree hX hη h₀ h₁ (Additive.ofMul a) = 0 := by
    rw [ofMul_zpow, map_zsmul, ha₀0, smul_zero]
  have han : a ^ n = 1 := by
    rw [← zpow_natCast, ← zpow_mul, mul_right_comm, mul_comm (d : ℤ) (n : ℤ), zpow_mul, zpow_mul,
      zpow_natCast, zpow_natCast, hadn, one_zpow]
  refine ⟨a, ⟨haK, ha0, han⟩, fun a' ⟨ha'K, ha'0, ha'n⟩ ↦ eq_of_mul_inv_eq_one ?_⟩
  exact toBase.eq_one_of_pullback_genericFiberι_eq_one_of_coprime_specialFiberMultiplicity
    K hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hconn hcop
    (by rw [LineBundleClass.pullback_mul, LineBundleClass.pullback_inv, ha'K, haK, mul_inv_cancel])
    (by rw [ofMul_mul, ofMul_inv, map_add, map_neg, ha'0, ha0, neg_zero, add_zero])
    (by rw [mul_pow, inv_pow, ha'n, han, inv_one, mul_one])

